Z||000000||Dan87GT||10-24-1999||10:10 AM||||    My '84 fiero is giving a trouble code 14 from the ECM right from start-up and does not turn off. I have changed the coolant temp. sensor and checked the wiring. The electric fan works perfectly.                Any Ideas???||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-24-1999||02:34 PM||||sounds like you changed the wrong temp sensor. the one for the fan & idiot light has nothing to do with the ECM.<P>I don't think many parts shops carry the ECM sensor. I tried a couple national ones and they couldn't even order it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||10-24-1999||02:56 PM||||Just bought an ECM temp sensor last week at Advance Auto Parts...$7.99.<P>Give 'em a try...if there isn't one in your town you might want to check for a website (sorry, don't know what it is.)||||reg||10
Z||000003||dans87gt||10-25-1999||07:14 AM||||This is on a 84 4 cylinder, I changed the sensor that is located on the thermostat housing,(the sensor that has the plastic cover over it), where is the ecm temp sensor??||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shipbuilder||10-26-1999||07:46 PM||||The one on the thermostat housing is for the ecm||||reg||1
